  "question": {
    "text": "In free space, a particle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> of charge <math><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#956;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> is held fixed&nbsp;at point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> . Another particle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> of the same charge and mass <math><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#956;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> is kept at a distance of <math><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>.</mo></math> If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> is released, then its velocity at a distance of <math><mn>9</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> is:<br />[Take <math><mi>&#160;</mi><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#1013;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>9</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>&#160;</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math> ]",
